+/* 5th.c in the style of Chicken Scheme ("Cheney on the M.T.A."): no tail calls, so every
+   dispatch is a real call that never returns and the C stack only grows.  DOCOL keeps its
+   return-stack frame {ip, parent, base} as a local on the C stack; EXIT resumes the parent's
+   ip.  Past STACK_BYTES, NEXT copies the frames still on the C stack into `heap` (a stack
+   itself, frames are never captured), fixes the parent pointers, parks the VM registers and
+   longjmps to main, which restarts on an empty stack.
+   >R, R>, RDROP and RSP@/RSP! use a shadow stack (env->rsp) of data only; `base` is its depth
+   when the frame was made, so EXIT can tell CATCH's pushed address (shadow < base: pop it,
+   stay) from a plain return (resume the parent, and keep exiting while shadow > its base,
+   which is how THROW's RSP! unwinds to CATCH).  `R0 RSP!` (QUIT) also drops every frame.
+   PRINT-STACK-TRACE finds nothing; a word that R>-drops its caller's address also drops
+   every enclosing frame of the same depth.
+   Build with -fno-optimize-sibling-calls or the compiler turns the calls back into jumps. */
